Z||000000||Cozmo||08-12-2001||07:13 AM||||Some cars come to mind...<BR>Fiat X/1-9...<BR> A great car to drive, the one I had started rusting out in 5 years tho.<BR>Triumph TR-7 (TR-8)...<BR> Triumph bet the farm on this one and lost. The 7 was underpowered and the 8 was SPOOKY to drive (I still want another one, tho).<BR>Toyota MR-2...<BR> Gen I only, with the right stuff these cars scream.<P>You can find nice examples of all of these cars for not very much $$$ (except for the TR-8). Imagine having one of each, in a matching color to your FIERO <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>BobC ||||reg||10
Z||000001||FieroBUZZ||08-12-2001||07:52 AM||||The most obvious is the AC 3000 from England (same company the Cobra came from) which appeared about 1972 and looks like where the Pontiac guys got a lot of styling ideas.<BR>Gary||||reg||6
Z||000002||85SE||08-12-2001||09:44 AM||||True story - a buddy of mine (who isn't really a car buff) once came over to my place and told me about this blue Fiero that was forsale down the street from him.  Said it was like a newer style than mine was.  I figured he meant the one blue 87 GT that's here in town and immediately went over to see it. Love blue GTs - really want one.<P>It was a 1988 Nissan Pulsar.  And it had a hole in the trunk.<P>Oh well. Next time maybe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I don't think we should add it to the list of cars though<P><P>------------------<BR>Andrew Menchions - 85SE - AKA Fieroless in Newfoundland||||reg||1
