Z||000016||HummelHund||08-12-2001||02:41 PM||||Two cars come to mind: the BMW M1 (from the front it sort of looks like a fiero with a kidney bean grille) and the AC Ghia. The AC Ghia was supposed to be a two seat midengined luxury car powered by a 3.0L V6, and is a dead ringer for a fastback Fiero GT with short sail panels. It even looks like it's got AusFiero's Stage 2 kit on it! I don't have a working scanner, but if anyone has a copy of the 1988 Motor Trend "How Ford Became #1" magazine it's on page 31. Very cool.<P><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6, The "Buzz Bomb". (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe, The "Black Wedge of Death" ($150 running car)||||reg||1
